$DIR/test.p:7:31: cannot use 1 << n (untyped int value) as Color value in return statement
    f is declared on line 7 to return Color, so it can only hold values of that
    type; 1 << n is an untyped int constant. Plutonium, like Go, does not
    convert between different types automatically.
    (see "Assignability" in the Plutonium spec, section 8.4)
    (run "pluto explain E0023" for a longer explanation)
